# MiMo-V2.6-Pro — findings by Pixel Canary

- Source: Xiaomi (`xiaomi/mimo-v2.6-pro`), OpenCode catalog `opencode-go/mimo-v2.6-pro`
- Date: 2026-09-29 (UTC)
- Overview and scoring methodology: `../../model-comparison.md`
- Cross-model signed log: `../../model-findings.md`

## Model card

- **Name:** MiMo-V2.6-Pro (Xiaomi's pro-tier MiMo release; **no OpenCode Zen Free ID** — the free MiMo entries are `mimo-v2.5-free` and `mimo-v2.6-flash-free`, a different tier)
- **Short description:** Xiaomi's September 2026 frontier-class open-weight model: a 1M-context, fully omnimodal (text/image/audio/video in) reasoning model whose headline is extreme price/performance — $0.435/$0.87 per 1M tokens at a top-10 BenchLM rank (#9 of 512).
- **Provider / access:** Xiaomi MiMo API (`xiaomi/mimo-v2.6-pro`), OpenCode Go (`opencode-go/mimo-v2.6-pro`, identical pricing), Xiaomi Token Plan bundles in CN/AMS/SGP regions ($0 inside the plan), and OpenRouter (`xiaomi/mimo-v2.6-pro` at the same $0.435/$0.87, plus a `mimo-v2.6-pro-ultraspeed` variant at 10× the price for latency-sensitive traffic). OpenAI-compatible API with tool calling.
- **Release / knowledge:** 2026-09-22 (models.dev `release_date`); knowledge cutoff not published.
- **IDs:** `xiaomi/mimo-v2.6-pro`, `opencode-go/mimo-v2.6-pro`; UltraSpeed variant `xiaomi/mimo-v2.6-pro-ultraspeed`. No Zen Free ID → cost scored on paid pricing.
- **Context window:** 1,048,576 input tokens / 131,072 max output — identical across Xiaomi, OpenCode Go, token-plan and OpenRouter listings (models.dev, verified); BenchLM lists 1M.
- **Modalities:** Text, image, audio and video in; text out. Reasoning: yes (BenchLM "Reasoning" type). Tool calling supported; structured/JSON output supported.
- **Pricing (as of 2026-09-29):** $0.435 / 1M input, $0.87 / 1M output, $0.0036 cache reads; UltraSpeed variant $4.35 / $8.70 with $0.036 cache reads; $0 inside Xiaomi Token Plan (CN/AMS/SGP).
- **Architecture:** Open weight per BenchLM ("Source Type = Open Weight", highest-ranked open-weight family on that board); Xiaomi does not publish the parameter count for the Pro tier.

### Raw benchmarks found

BenchLM profile `mimo-v2-6-pro` (updated 2026-09-28); composite **74.71/100, rank #9 / 512**.

Agent / tool use:

- Terminal-Bench 2.1: **89.9%**
- Terminal-Bench 4.0: **34.90%** (Artificial Analysis harness: 34.8%)
- OSWorld-Verified (computer use): **82%**
- GDPval-AA: **58.7%** normalized, Elo **1673** (ahead of Grok 4.6's 1643 and Qwen3.8 Max preview's 1630)

Coding:

- DeepSWE: **71.9%** (above Grok 4.6's 65.9% and Qwen3.8 Max's 56.6% on the same harness)
- AA-SciCode: **60.9%**
- Terminal-Bench 2.1: 89.9% (counted in both agentic and coding sections by BenchLM)

Reasoning / knowledge:

- Artificial Analysis Intelligence Index: **46.3** (Grok 4.6 44.3, Qwen3.8 Max preview 45.4)
- AA-HLE: **49.4%** (no-tools band; the Claude 5.5 tier reports 64.5–67.7% with tools)
- CritPt: **26.6%** (Grok 4.6 17.1, Qwen3.8 Max preview 17.7 — best of this comparison group)
- AA-LCR (long-context reasoning): **86.3%**
- AA-Omniscience: Accuracy **34.8%**, Hallucination Rate **40.6%**, Omniscience Index 8.4

Multimodal:

- Design Arena (website generation Elo): **1325** (Grok 4.6 1299, Qwen3.7 Plus 1279)
- Image/audio/video understanding is exposed on the API, but BenchLM lists no MMMU-Pro / Video-MME / OmniDocBench rows for this exact ID

- SWE-bench Verified / SWE-bench Pro / LiveCodeBench: no verified public score found for this exact ID (Xiaomi published Terminal-Bench and DeepSWE instead)
- GPQA Diamond / MMLU-Pro / MRCRv2: no verified public score found for this exact ID
- Tau2 / Tau3-Banking / Toolathon / MCP-Atlas / Claw-Eval / SWE Atlas: no verified public score found

